cff-version: 1.2.0
title: "Kronos Quantum — honest, runnable quantum-computing-for-fusion codes"
message: "If you use this software, please cite it."
type: software
authors:
  - name: "Kronos Fusion Energy"
version: "0.3.0"
license: Apache-2.0
repository-code: "https://github.com/KronosFE/kronos-quantum"
keywords:
  - fusion
  - quantum computing
  - VQE
  - QAOA
  - quantum machine learning
  - error mitigation
abstract: >
  Nine runnable quantum programs for fusion problems — variational quantum
  eigensolver, quantum kernels, QAOA, Trotterized dynamics, fault-tolerant
  resource estimation, quantum metrology, tensor-network compression, error
  mitigation, and a variational quantum linear solver. Each executes on a free
  local simulator today and on real quantum hardware the moment a backend is
  configured, on one code path. No quantum advantage is claimed this decade; a
  meaningful role in fusion is a post-~2036 prospect. The tooling and testing
  are real now.
references:
  - type: data
    title: "CGYRO nonlinear kinetic-electron turbulence flux data (A1e map)"
